// markdownlint-cli2 configuration (issue #243).
//
// markdownlint-cli2 reads this file as its CLI options file. Rule
// settings are nested under the "config" key (flat rule keys here would
// be silently ignored as unknown options); "ignores" stays top-level.
//
// All markdownlint default rules are on except where "config" overrides
// them. Each override documents a deliberate, repo-wide choice rather
// than a per-file exception:
//
// MD013 (line-length): 120 characters, code blocks and tables exempt.
//   Prose wraps well under the limit, but code fences and padded table
//   cells routinely exceed it, and rewrapping them would break them or
//   their alignment.
// MD060 (table-column-style): off. Repo tables use padded cells with
//   compact |---| separators; the rule is style-only with no rendering
//   effect, and forcing one alignment would churn every table in the repo.
// MD033 (inline-html): off. MkDocs pages deliberately use inline HTML
//   (details/summary, anchors) that markdownlint does not model.
//
// AGENTS.md is excluded (top-level "ignores"): it is an agent-managed
// file with an owner-curated layout, and rewrapping it for line length
// is out of scope for the documentation style gate.
//
// Generated directories are ignored as well: markdownlint-cli2 does not
// read .gitignore, and a local run after `uv sync` or `mise run
// docs-build` would otherwise sweep .venv/ and build/ into the lint.
{
  "config": {
    "MD013": {
      "line_length": 120,
      "code_blocks": false,
      "tables": false
    },
    "MD060": false,
    "MD033": false
  },
  "ignores": [
    "AGENTS.md",
    ".venv/**",
    "build/**",
    ".hermes/**",
    ".wip/**",
    ".setup/**",
    "airgap/archives/**",
    "airgap/rendered/**",
    "airgap/sbom/**",
    "airgap/config-artifact/**"
  ]
}
